INT. ORBITAL SALVAGE TUG "LONG PATIENCE," CARGO BAY - SHIP NIGHT

Strip lighting. Mag-boots clank. Crates stacked in nets. A viewport shows a wreck turning slowly against the stars.

OKSANA REYNOLDS-ADEBOYE (40s, engineer, grease up to the elbows) crouches over an open hatch, a wrench in one hand. She does not look up when the intercom hisses.

COMMS (V.O.)
Engineer. Bridge. Report.

She keeps working. Turns a bolt. Another.

OKSANA
Still on it.

COMMS (V.O.)
Captain wants a status on the coupling.

OKSANA
Tell the Captain it's a coupling.

COMMS (V.O.)
Copy.

She sets the wrench down. Wipes her hands on her thighs. From a vent behind her, a soft click.

She turns slowly. Nothing. But she picks the wrench back up.

A second figure floats in from the airlock: SIMEON AKINTOLA-VEGA (30s, flight tech, jumpsuit unzipped to the chest). He anchors himself with one boot to a crate and stares at her.

SIMEON
You okay?

OKSANA
Fine.

SIMEON
You've been down here nine hours.

OKSANA
It's a big coupling.

SIMEON
Captain says come up.

OKSANA
Captain says what?

COMMS (V.O.)
Engineer, Captain says come up. Immediately.

OKSANA
(to the intercom)
Why?

COMMS (V.O.)
Something on the scanner. Something near the wreck.

Oksana and Simeon look at each other. She tightens her grip on the wrench. He zips his jumpsuit to the collar.

SIMEON
What is it?

COMMS (V.O.)
Unknown. Moving. Matching our heading.

OKSANA
How close?

COMMS (V.O.)
Twelve kilometers. And closing.

She lets the wrench drift. It spins slowly in front of her, catching the light.

SIMEON
I'm going up.

OKSANA
Wait.

He waits. Her eyes go to the viewport. The wreck rotates; behind it, a shape too regular to be debris.

She says nothing. Neither does he. They float side by side.

COMMS (V.O.)
Engineer? Tech? Respond.

Simeon opens his mouth. Closes it. Oksana presses the intercom.

OKSANA
(evenly)
We're coming up.

She lets go. Drifts across the bay. At the door she stops, lays one palm flat on a crate as if for luck.

Then she follows Simeon into the corridor.
